,title,link,text,language,family
0,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Tilung,Sino-Tibetan
1,"Tibetan Music | Himalayan Temple | Instrumental Asian MusicTibetan Singing Bowl Music, Singing Bowl for Meditation ...Tibetan Music & Audio — Stream & Download Traditional Music ...Stream tilung Tilung music | Listen to songs, albums ...Tibetan Traditional Music: Folk Song, Sacred Chant, HeritageTilung language — GrokipediaMusic of Tibet - Wikipedia",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J9dAmDy3jWE,"Dec 22, 2017 · If you're interested in hearing more relaxing music please check out the first song I've written for my new relaxing music channel, Relax & Vibe, here: https... Oct 27, 2025 · Tibetan Singing Bowl Music | Singing Bowl for Meditation & Healing | Singing Bowl Sound Therapy Immerse yourself in the sacred resonance of Tibetan singing bowls, designed to promote... Stream rare recordings of traditional Tibetan instruments, monastic chanting, and contemporary Tibetan artists. Play tilung Tilung and discover followers on SoundCloud | Stream tracks, albums, playlists on desktop and mobile. It is generally divided into five main types: folk music, dance music, rap music, opera music, and instrumental music. These categories reflect the versatility and creativity of Tibetan artists, each contributing distinct elements to the cultural landscape. The Tilung language, a member of the Kiranti subgroup of Sino-Tibetan languages spoken in eastern Nepal, features a consonant inventory of 25 phonemes, characterized by contrasts in voicing, aspiration, and breathy voicing across stops and affricates. The soundtrack to Kundun, by Philip Glass, has helped to popularize Tibetan music. Foreign styles of popular music have also had a major impact within the Tibetan diaspora, where Indian ghazal and filmi are very popular and American rock has produced the India-based Rangzen Shonu.",Tilung,Sino-Tibetan
